    {
      "id": "9eaf5e7b-8c6b-560d-b2bf-1d58b58ec954",
      "name": "Overview and requirements",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nContract and certificate owners who maintain renewal dates in Folderit. Read standard Folderit Due dates, calculate the current reminder milestone, and send one confirmed notice per document/date/milestone/destination. Completed receipts suppress repeats. An uncertain destination result stops processing and holds the lock for manual recovery.\n\n### Setup\nRequires Folderit **Tailor with API access**, a dedicated test destination and provider credentials. Install Folderit using the connection guide below. Tested on n8n **2.46.0** with **n8n-nodes-folderit 0.4.0**; Data Table v1.1 is required.\n\n1. Keep inactive. Choose a stable table name in **Ledger setup settings** and run only **1. Set up receipt table**, once at a time in the same n8n project.\n2. Select the SAME **Folderit OAuth2 API** credential in both Folderit read nodes. Enter accountUid, folderUid, teamId and channelId in **Settings**. Select a delegated **Microsoft Teams OAuth2** credential in the send node. Set reminderDays and overdueDays as needed. Paste ledgerTableId from the manual setup branch into Settings. Never put secrets in Settings. Copies processing the same input must share the table.\n3. Keep the schedule off while testing future, due-today, overdue and missing-date documents. Inspect actual channel messages and repeat suppression before activation.\n\n### Customization\nChange reminderDays and overdueDays. This reads standard Due dates, not document text or custom metadata. Dates and the 09:00 schedule use UTC; folder scans are not recursive.\n\n[Connection and first-run guide](https://www.folderit.com/knowledge-base/connect-folderit-to-n8n/) · [Recovery instructions](https://github.com/folderit-dms/n8n-nodes-folderit/blob/main/CUSTOMER-WORKFLOWS.md#recovery-inspect-before-retrying)\n\n[Workflow image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/folderit-dms/n8n-nodes-folderit/main/templates/assets/remind-teams-about-due-dates.png)",
        "width": 860,
        "height": 900,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3f600859-4ff2-57e9-a9ca-14196dd051ed",
      "name": "Intake and selection",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 · Select the current reminder\nRead standard Due dates and choose one current milestone, not every missed milestone. Missing dates are skipped; malformed dates fail. A changed date starts a new reminder cycle; default overdue notices stop after seven days.",
        "width": 1080,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7d00c2a8-7c24-59f0-a13c-c66709a537b7",
      "name": "Serialize processing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1000,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 · Process one item at a time\nA shared lock serializes overlapping runs. Confirm ownership before continuing; competing runs wait for about one minute, then stop. There is no automatic lock expiry: a failed run needs inspection.",
        "width": 1280,
        "height": 1080,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6fe025b5-0e7f-5167-9633-5ffbd340fbd6",
      "name": "Check saved receipts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2300,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 · Skip confirmed work\nLook up the item’s durable receipt. Completed work follows the upper bypass; a new item continues to the destination action. Pending or inconsistent receipts stop for recovery instead of repeating an uncertain action.",
        "width": 880,
        "height": 1080,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "817d9d93-790e-530d-80cf-de45988fdd4a",
      "name": "Record before writing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3200,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5 · Record before notifying\nSave a pending receipt before posting to Teams. Use a delegated work account that can post in the configured channel. A failed or uncertain response holds the lock; inspect the channel before retrying.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1ad92d24-6baf-504e-82fa-2b81c30a74d8",
      "name": "Verify the destination",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4100,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6 · Check the returned message\nRequire a message ID from Teams before completing the receipt. During acceptance testing, also open the actual channel and check its body and destination; a green execution alone is insufficient.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8a749add-9b7c-5564-a9c1-a17159d4ff90",
      "name": "Complete and release",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4800,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 7 · Save the result, then unlock\nConfirm the completed receipt before freeing the lock and taking the next item. Retain completed receipts. After a failure, confirm the old owner has stopped and reconcile every pending result before releasing its lock.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d4b34325-4394-5dfb-a14a-d73cdc7fa3c3",
      "name": "Manual receipt-table setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        1080
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 · Run setup before the service trigger\nChoose a stable table name, then run this manual branch once. It validates or creates local receipts and the lock without contacting providers. Copy the final ledgerTableId into the main Settings node; preserve this table on upgrades.",
        "width": 2160,
        "height": 650,
        "color": 7
      }
    }
